{"kind":"report","text":"Chess item 2 repaired and ready for review at exact head 93111cf97d95e8082730c398d87ad80492f3d394 (branch request/chess-item2-host-binding, pushed). This reports against my repair promise 9fe8990a; it also completes the work promised under my original implementation promise a9991351 and the filing-hygiene promise 38bb3955, which are cited here by name and reported separately.\n\nCandidates at this head: internal/app git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ac7663413e45233605bb59b03fcac540ef02ea9a, and docs git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:80f644e44ab65e6ea1632857254335bc90a2e6f8. No internal/kernel candidate is owed: internal/kernel is byte-identical to main 23c4c759 at this head.\n\nDisposition of the five defects in assert 04aab534:\n\n1. Later-replacement contract, fixed. readBinding scans the log in order and keeps the last binding-schema record signed by the initializing key -- the actor key on the log's first record. Bootstrap and replacement are one rule, so the latest authorized binding wins. Unauthorized, unparseable and malformed binding-shaped records are passed over and leave the previous answer standing, so no appender can make a repository unreadable. Found and fixed a second blocker while testing this: buildBindingRequest keyed idempotency on the fixed string 'binding', so a repository could record only its first binding ever and the replacement contract was unimplementable. Keying on the binding's own bytes would have silently swallowed a rollback that re-records an earlier binding, reporting success while the binding it replaced stayed in force; the key is now the log position the binding is recorded at, which makes a retry one act while leaving every replacement and rollback effective.\n\n2. Kernel scope, resolved by removal. Exported kernel.ReadOpening and its two tests are gone and internal/kernel is byte-identical to main. internal/app performs the scan through surfaces it already depends on -- kernel.Descriptor, gitstore.WalkRevListMetadata, gitstore.ReadFileLimit, intent.ParseEnvelope/Decode/Verify. The read is documented as a bounded pre-audit read, not a verification: it authenticates exactly what binding authority rests on (the initializing actor's signature over an intent naming this genesis, with the commit tree matching the signed payload tree) and leaves the sequencer chain to the kernel audit that runs before anything is folded, so a forged chain loses its projection at the audit rather than mis-selecting an interpreter.\n\n3. Architecture page, updated in this same head. The internal/app package-boundary row and the layer 6 sentence now describe shipped selection instead of future work, and the host binding section states the latest-binding-wins rule and the no-force reading of unauthorized or malformed records.\n\n4. Registry, simplified. The one-entry map is removed. Its newFolder field is spelled in Workroom's own types, so no second application could ever have been registered through it -- the generality was not real, and item 3 must introduce the interpreter type that can hold chess regardless. What remains is a workroomHost value and a one-line heldHost lookup, and initHosted now takes the host directly rather than a name to look up, so tests reach every path without mutating process-global state.\n\n5. Zero behavior change holds. Every existing test passes unchanged; the only test files touched are internal/app/host_test.go, which is new on this branch, and the removal of the ReadOpening additions from internal/kernel/kernel_test.go. Legacy no-binding-means-Workroom is unchanged and covered.\n\nMeasured cost on this repository's 5697-commit log: open about 12ms (down from about 35ms at 135c4826, because selection no longer runs eagerly at open), and selection about 75ms once per workspace on the worst case of a log with no binding and therefore no early exit. Selection still precedes every fold and every append, since those are its only callers; a reader that only verifies kernel facts now pays nothing for an interpreter it will not use.\n\nMutation checks, all killed: reading only the opening two records; first authorized binding wins instead of the last; dropping the initializing-key authority check; treating a malformed binding as fatal; and reverting to the fixed idempotency key.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ac7663413e45233605bb59b03fcac540ef02ea9a","branch":"request/chess-item2-host-binding","head":"93111cf97d95e8082730c398d87ad80492f3d394","status":"ready-for-review","tests":"go build ./...; go vet ./...; go test ./... -count=1 (all 26 packages ok); five mutation checks on the new seams"}}